       <h1>72-Year-Old Vidya Singh Scales Mt Kilimanjaro</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#positive</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Vidya Singh, 72, has become one of the oldest Indians to summit Mount Kilimanjaro, reaching the 5,895-metre Uhuru Peak on March 13, 2025. A lifelong fitness enthusiast, Singh began high-altitude trekking at age 59 and has since completed 19 expeditions.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-02/72-year-old-vidya-singh-scales-mt-kilimanjaro.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Her Kilimanjaro ascent involved a demanding week-long climb and a difficult descent over muddy, rocky terrain. Despite falling multiple times, Singh successfully completed the trek and continues to maintain a rigorous training regimen. She credits her success to a lifelong commitment to physical fitness and emphasizes the importance of approaching mountain climbing with an open mind.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately summarizes the key details of Vidya Singh's achievement and training, capturing the essential facts from the provided source.</p>
