       <h1>Abhishek Sharma Reportedly Unhappy at Sunrisers Hyderabad and Seeks IPL Exit Ahead of Retention Deadline</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Abhishek Sharma's future with Sunrisers Hyderabad has drawn intense focus ahead of the upcoming IPL retention deadline. The opening batter is reportedly unhappy after Ishan Kishan was given the captaincy last year. Kishan is expected to continue in that leadership role for IPL 2027 because Pat Cummins is likely to reduce his franchise cricket commitments.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-02/abhishek-sharma-reportedly-unhappy-at-sunrisers-hyderabad-an.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>As speculation grows regarding his departure, several potential destinations have emerged for the star batter. Mumbai Indians, Gujarat Titans, and Punjab Kings are among the interested teams, while the Delhi Capitals could also surface as a viable option for Sharma.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft accurately captures all the key details regarding Abhishek Sharma's situation and potential future destinations mentioned in the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/sports/cricket/ipl/top-stories/ipl-retentions-unhappy-abhishek-sharma-wants-to-leave-srh-but-where-will-he-go/articleshow/134638490.cms" rel="noopener">Times of India</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
