     <article class="story single" data-beat="entertainment">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">ENTERTAINMENT</span> · TOI Entertainment · 2026-10-02 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Ajay Devgn's 'Drishyam 3: The Conclusion' draws mixed X reactions</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Drishyam3</span> <span>#AjayDevgn</span> <span>#Bollywood</span></div>
       <p>Ajay Devgn returns as Vijay Salgaonkar in &quot;Drishyam 3: The Conclusion&quot;, the third Hindi installment directed by Abhishek Pathak. Tabu, Shriya Saran, Ishita Dutta and Rajat Kapoor reprise their roles while Prakash Raj and Jaideep Ahlawat join the cast.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-02/ajay-devgns-drishyam-3-the-conclusion-draws-mixed-x-reaction.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Early reactions on X highlight the film’s suspense, twists and especially the climax and interval sequence. One user wrote, &quot;Drishyam 3 has proved that a good movie requires neither bikini scenes nor item numbers nor a big budget nor a foreign location,&quot; while another praised the climax twist as &quot;BETTER than Drishyam 1 and 2&quot; and called the interval &quot;MIND BLOWING&quot;.</p><p>A contrasting voice called the movie a &quot;predictable family thriller&quot; and said the Hindi version &quot;fails to match part 1&quot; of the Malayalam original, though it noted that Jaideep Ahlawat and Prakash Raj shine.</p><p>Critics on X lauded Pathak’s direction and writing; one reviewer gave four‑and‑a‑half stars, calling it the &quot;BEST FILM in the Drishyam franchise&quot; and a &quot;SURE‑SHOT BLOCKBUSTER&quot;. Another gave four out of five stars, describing it as &quot;BRILLIANT&quot; and &quot;Even better than Part two and one&quot;.</p><p>What to watch: audience split between praise for the climax and criticism of predictability.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft effectively captures the varying audience reactions and critic reviews from the source material.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/entertainment/hindi/bollywood/news/drishyam-3-x-review-ajay-devgns-thriller-gets-praise-for-climax-and-twists-netizens-say-we-are-not-ready-for-the-climax/articleshow/134632918.cms" rel="noopener">TOI Entertainment</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
