       <h1>Akhilesh Yadav signals potential alliance for Rajya Sabha polls</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Samajwadi Party chief Akhilesh Yadav has called for unity ahead of the upcoming Rajya Sabha elections, suggesting a willingness to collaborate with former associates. Yadav’s remarks follow reports that the Samajwadi Party intends to field a third candidate for the 10-seat election in Uttar Pradesh, potentially triggering cross-voting.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-02/akhilesh-yadav-signals-potential-alliance-for-rajya-sabha-po.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>While the BJP-led alliance is positioned to win seven seats, the SP-Congress coalition currently holds enough strength for two. SP leaders have claimed some BJP MLAs are interested in switching sides for the 2027 Assembly elections. Nominations for the Rajya Sabha polls close on October 6, with scrutiny scheduled for the following day.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article effectively captures the political maneuvering regarding the Rajya Sabha elections and the numerical breakdown of the assembly.</p>
