     <article class="story single" data-beat="entertainment">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">ENTERTAINMENT</span> · Bollywood Hungama · 2026-10-02 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Alia Bhatt Reunites with F1 Star Carlos Sainz for L’Oréal Campaign</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Bollywood</span> <span>#Formula 1</span> <span>#Advertising</span></div>
       <p>Bollywood actress Alia Bhatt and Formula 1 driver Carlos Sainz have reunited for a new L’Oréal advertisement, months after their notable meeting at the Cannes Film Festival earlier this year. The collaboration, promoting the brand’s new Elvive haircare range, has recently surfaced on social media and is circulating widely among fans.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-02/alia-bhatt-reunites-with-f1-star-carlos-sainz-for-loreal-cam.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The advertisement, which appears to be an Italian promotional campaign, features Bhatt and Sainz together. Their initial encounter at Cannes had generated considerable online interest, sparking speculation about a potential professional partnership. The new campaign confirms this possibility, eliciting an enthusiastic response from fans online.</p><p>On the professional front, Alia Bhatt recently headlined &quot;Alpha&quot; within the YRF Spy Universe and saw &quot;Don’t Be Shy&quot; premiere on Amazon Prime Video. Her upcoming projects include Sanjay Leela Bhansali’s &quot;Love &amp; War,&quot; co-starring Ranbir Kapoor and Vicky Kaushal, slated for release in January next year. She has also completed work on &quot;Tumbbad 2&quot; and recently featured with Ranbir Kapoor in Myntra’s Big Fashion Festival campaign.</p><p>What to watch: Alia Bhatt's upcoming film &quot;Love &amp; War&quot; in January next year.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article effectively summarizes the source, including the context of the L'Oréal ad and the actress's professional slate.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.bollywoodhungama.com/news/features/alia-bhatt-reunites-with-f1-star-carlos-sainz-for-loreal-ad-after-cannes-meeting-video-goes-viral/" rel="noopener">Bollywood Hungama</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
