     <article class="story single" data-beat="tech">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">TECH</span> · The Verge · 2026-10-02 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Amazon Warns Against Blocking AI Data Centers in Blog Post</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Amazon</span> <span>#AI Data Centers</span> <span>#Policy</span></div>
       <p>Amazon Web Services CEO Matt Garman published a 3,000-word blog post urging communities to support AI data center projects, warning that opposition risks irreparable harm to the US economy and national security. Garman argued that the US cannot afford to lose the race for AI dominance and suggested that foreign entities are seeding misinformation to slow down domestic buildout.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-02/amazon-warns-against-blocking-ai-data-centers-in-blog-post.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The memorandum, titled the &quot;Data Center Commitment,&quot; outlines practices including job creation, preventing local energy rate increases, and investing over $1 billion in neighboring communities. Amazon also disclosed it no longer uses nondisclosure agreements with government agencies, a change following probes by Democratic lawmaker Jamie Raskin.</p><p>This defense comes amid declining public support for data centers, with over 100 moratoriums currently under consideration across the US. In related comments, Amazon’s chief global affairs officer David Zapolsky stated that the industry’s history of secrecy was reflexive and that transparency with community leaders is now essential.</p><p>What to watch: The outcome of the 100+ local moratoriums being considered and potential regulatory responses to the transparency pledge.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft accurately synthesizes the source material, capturing the core arguments and specific policy commitments mentioned in the text.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.theverge.com/tech/1003929/amazon-ai-data-center-blog-warning" rel="noopener">The Verge</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
