     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · News18 India · 2026-10-02 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Amit Shah Praises Putin’s Commendation of PM Modi’s Peace Efforts</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Union Home Minister Amit Shah called Russian President Vladimir Putin’s praise for Prime Minister Narendra Modi’s global peace efforts a &quot;moment of pride&quot; for India. Shah noted that the commendation, arriving on Mahatma Gandhi’s birth anniversary, solidifies India's status as a trusted voice for peace under Modi's leadership.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-02/amit-shah-praises-putins-commendation-of-pm-modis-peace-effo.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The Russian President recently acknowledged that PM Modi frequently raises the necessity of ending the Ukraine conflict during their diplomatic discussions. Putin highlighted this stance despite the two leaders maintaining friendly bilateral relations.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft accurately captures the essence of the report, though it slightly conflates the timeline of the Ukraine conflict, citing it as in its fifth year rather than the specific event context.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
