       <h1>Aviation Experts Analyze Flydubai Cockpit Incident</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Captain C.S. Randhawa, president of the Federation of Indian Pilots, has categorized the recent Flydubai cockpit attack as an extremely serious aviation event. In a discussion regarding the incident on flight FZ1073, Randhawa emphasized that the physical altercation between the pilots requires a comprehensive investigation. The captain’s quick thinking and actions remain a central focus of the ongoing inquiry.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-02/aviation-experts-analyze-flydubai-cockpit-incident.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Captain Smit Machchhar, while recovering in an Abu Dhabi hospital, confirmed to Prime Minister Narendra Modi that he managed to open the cockpit door despite suffering severe injuries. This action allowed others to intervene during the flight. Aviation experts and authorities continue to examine the circumstances surrounding the attack.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Very accurate summary of the provided text, capturing the expert's stance and the pilot's account.</p>
