     <article class="story single" data-beat="positive">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">POSITIVE</span> · Good News Network · 2026-10-02 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>BHP wins BC Reclamation Award for 30-year Island Copper Mine cleanup</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#BHP</span> <span>#Island Copper Mine</span> <span>#British Columbia</span> <span>#Reclamation</span></div>
       <p>BHP received the Annual Reclamation Award from the BC Technical Research Committee on Reclamation for its ongoing work at the former Island Copper Mine near Port Hardy, British Columbia. The honor recognizes three decades of monitoring and maintenance efforts that have restored the site since the mine closed in 1995.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-02/bhp-wins-bc-reclamation-award-for-30-year-island-copper-mine.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The mine, which operated from 1971 to 1995, contained over 1 billion tons of ore and employed 900 residents at its peak, growing Port Hardy into a town of 5,000. To manage the environmental impact of the 1,320-foot deep pit, BHP flooded it with seawater to create a stratified lake that neutralizes acid rock drainage.</p><p>Since May 2001, the company has fertilized the surface waters every 7–10 days to stimulate plankton blooms. These blooms absorb heavy metals and oxygen, preventing mineral oxidation and protecting the water system. The TRCR noted that these efforts have enhanced environmental protection and improved the site's resilience to extreme weather.</p><p>Why it matters: Proactive reclamation transforms hazardous industrial sites into stable, monitored ecosystems.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft effectively integrates all the facts from the source text into a coherent news story.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.goodnewsnetwork.org/30-years-of-clean-up-and-monitoring-work-at-closed-copper-mine-wins-honors-for-worlds-top-miner/" rel="noopener">Good News Network</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
