     <article class="story single" data-beat="finance">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">FINANCE</span> · Livemint Money · 2026-10-02 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Central Government Employees Anticipate DA Hike Before Dussehra</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#finance</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Central government employees and pensioners are expecting a 3-4% Dearness Allowance (DA) hike for the July 2026 cycle, with a formal announcement anticipated before the Dussehra festival. This adjustment would raise the current 60% rate to 63-64%, benefiting approximately 50 lakh employees and 69 lakh pensioners.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-02/central-government-employees-anticipate-da-hike-before-dusse.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The expectation follows a rise in the All-India Consumer Price Index for Industrial Workers (AICPI-IW) to 154.4 in August 2026. While the revision is effective retroactively from July 1, the government has yet to release the final figures. Employee unions have urged the Department of Expenditure to expedite the process to include the arrears in October's salary.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Thoroughly covers the DA hike expectations, numbers, and background data from the text.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.livemint.com/money/da-hike-for-central-govt-employees-can-pensioners-and-workers-expect-a-raise-for-july-cycle-before-dussehra-11790925280592.html" rel="noopener">Livemint Money</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
