     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · News18 India · 2026-10-02 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Cockroach Janta Party Stages Protest at Shivaji Park</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The Cockroach Janta Party (CJP), led by founder Abhijeet Dipke, held a ‘Season 2’ protest at Mumbai’s Shivaji Park on Friday to demand the resignation of Chief Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar. The demonstration follows allegations of irregularities during the Special Intensive Revision of electoral rolls.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-02/cockroach-janta-party-stages-protest-at-shivaji-park.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Maharashtra Chief Minister Devendra Fadnavis dismissed the protests as a push for a “fake narrative” already debunked by the Election Commission. While police cited a 2013 High Court order regarding silence zones to deny formal gathering permission, Dipke has vowed to expand the movement nationwide.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article effectively synthesizes the protest details, the political context, and the specific police stance regarding the venue.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.news18.com/india/abhijeet-dipke-leads-cjps-protest-at-mumbais-shivaji-park-fadnavis-slams-fake-narrative-ws-r-10364800.html" rel="noopener">News18 India</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
