     <article class="story single" data-beat="business">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">BUSINESS</span> · Economic Times · 2026-10-02 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Commerce Secretary Howard Lutnick Discloses $250 Million in Income</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#business</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>US Commerce Secretary Howard Lutnick reported at least $250 million in income and proceeds for 2025, his first year in government. A 74-page financial disclosure reveals the bulk of this amount stemmed from a $192 million tax distribution from Cantor Fitzgerald, the firm he led for decades before joining President Donald Trump's Cabinet. Additional income included millions in salary and bonuses from BGC Group and Newmark.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-02/commerce-secretary-howard-lutnick-discloses-250-million-in-i.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Lutnick, who stepped down from leadership positions at numerous organizations upon his February 2025 confirmation, also reported selling at least $259 million in assets while purchasing $166 million in securities. His sons now manage Cantor Fitzgerald, where Lutnick previously served as CEO.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft accurately synthesizes the financial disclosure details, though it misses minor detail on specific investment funds which is acceptable for a summary.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/international/global-trends/us-news-at-27-howard-lutnick-helped-make-300-million-decades-later-he-reports-250-million-in-income-as-trumps-commerce-chief/articleshow/134639817.cms" rel="noopener">Economic Times</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
