     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · India Today · 2026-10-02 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Couple Found Dead in Bahraich Hotel Room</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>A 46-year-old married woman from Noida and her 27-year-old partner were found hanging in a Bahraich hotel room on Friday. The pair, identified as Pinky and Rinku, had checked into the hotel on September 22 posing as a married couple. The hotel operator alerted police after noticing no activity in the room throughout the day.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-02/couple-found-dead-in-bahraich-hotel-room.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Police discovered the bodies after forcing entry into the room. An FSL team is investigating the scene, and the bodies have been sent for post-mortem examinations. While authorities suspect suicide, the exact circumstances and motives behind the deaths remain under investigation as officials review call records and family statements.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Concise and accurate reporting of the incident details provided in the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.indiatoday.in/india/story/bahraich-hotel-deaths-noida-woman-partner-found-hanging-ptag-3007971-2026-10-02?utm_source=rss" rel="noopener">India Today</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
