     <article class="story single" data-beat="sports">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">SPORTS</span> · BBC Sport · 2026-10-02 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Cyclist Ronan Auge in medically induced coma after crash</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#sports</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>French cyclist Ronan Auge has been placed in a medically induced coma following a serious crash at the Tour of Langkawi in Malaysia. The 22-year-old suffered injuries during stage six of the UCI ProSeries event and remains under medical care.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-02/cyclist-ronan-auge-in-medically-induced-coma-after-crash.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>His team, Unibet Red Roses, described his condition as stable and not life-threatening. The incident adds to a recent string of high-profile cycling accidents, including the death of Fin Tarling in August and the hospitalization of Ezra Caudell last month. The Tour of Langkawi is scheduled to conclude this Sunday.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article is concise and accurately reflects the source material, though it omits the specific detail of the crash occurring between Pandan Indah and Rembau.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
