       <h1>De Luca and Abdy to Leave Warner Bros. Following Paramount Merger</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#entertainment</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Warner Bros. chiefs Michael De Luca and Pamela Abdy are set to depart their roles following the completion of the $110 billion merger between Paramount Skydance and Warner Bros. Discovery. Multiple sources confirmed that the duo will not be included in David Ellison’s future management team.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-02/de-luca-and-abdy-to-leave-warner-bros-following-paramount-me.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The leadership change follows the finalized terms of the landmark deal. De Luca and Abdy’s tenure concludes as the company prepares for a new administrative structure under Ellison’s direction once the transaction officially closes.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article is accurate and captures the core information provided in the source summary.</p>
