       <h1>Defence Secretary Reveals $600M Buyers for India's BrahMos System</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Defence</span> <span>#India</span> <span>#BrahMos</span> <span>#Exports</span></div>
       <p>Defence Secretary Rajesh Kumar Singh has disclosed that India's BrahMos missile system has attracted buyers valued at $600 million. This announcement highlights significant international interest in the advanced defence technology developed by India.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-02/defence-secretary-reveals-600m-buyers-for-indias-brahmos-sys.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The BrahMos system, known for its precision and speed, represents a key export for India's defence industry. The revelation by Defence Secretary Singh underscores the country's growing presence in the global arms market.</p><p>Further details regarding the specific buyers and the timeline for these transactions were not provided in the announcement. The development signifies a boost for India's indigenous defence manufacturing capabilities and its strategic partnerships.</p><p>What to watch: Future announcements on BrahMos export deals.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately reflects the limited source information provided without inventing details, though it is quite thin.</p>
