     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-02 · editor 6/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Delhi Police Restrict Protests Against CEC Gyanesh Kumar</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Authorities have heightened security and suspended internet services around Delhi’s Jantar Mantar following a denied protest permit against Chief Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar. Police barricaded the site and detained Aam Aadmi Party leader Saurabh Bharadwaj as crowds gathered on Gandhi Jayanti.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-02/delhi-police-restrict-protests-against-cec-gyanesh-kumar.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Delhi Traffic Police issued an advisory warning of diversions near Connaught Place and Parliament Street, urging commuters to avoid the area. Concurrently, Citizens for Justice and Peace founder Abhijeet Dipke faces similar restrictions for a planned demonstration at Mumbai’s Shivaji Park, as activists continue to demand the CEC’s resignation.</p>
       
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/cec-gyanesh-kumar-row-cjp-opposition-parties-to-organise-separate-protests-live-updates-october-2-2026/article71535655.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       <div class="cityguide"><b>City guide</b><p>More on <a href="https://bharatdn.com/city/delhi/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Delhi</a> - census 2011 population, live weather and air quality, local food and getaways.</p></div>
