       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">ENTERTAINMENT</span> · TOI Entertainment · 2026-10-02 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Dino Morea Arrested in Mithi River Desilting Scam Over Rs 65.54 Crore Loss</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Dino Morea</span> <span>#Mithi River</span> <span>#Mumbai Police</span></div>
       <p>Mumbai Police’s Economic Offences Wing arrested actor Dino Morea after a lengthy questioning session. The arrest is linked to the alleged Mithi River desilting scam that involved financial irregularities in contracts awarded for the river’s rejuvenation. The Brihanmumbai Municipal Corporation reportedly suffered a loss of Rs 65.54 crore due to those contracts. Morea had previously been questioned in May 2025 over phone records that connected him to the investigation.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-02/dino-morea-arrested-in-mithi-river-desilting-scam-over-rs-65.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>What to watch: further developments in the Mithi River case and potential charges against involved parties.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft perfectly captures all key facts from the summary, including the specific financial loss and the context of the investigation.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/entertainment/hindi/bollywood/news/dino-morea-arrested-by-mumbai-polices-eow-in-mithi-river-desilting-case-over-loss-of-rs-65-54-crore-suffered-by-bmc-after-8-hours-of-questioning/articleshow/134638063.cms" rel="noopener">TOI Entertainment</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
