     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-02 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>ECI Orders BLOs to Re-enroll Eligible Voters Omitted from Lists</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The Election Commission of India (ECI) has directed Booth Level Officers (BLOs) to compare pre-Special Intensive Revision (SIR) voter lists with current records to identify eligible electors who were inadvertently left out. BLOs must conduct house-to-house visits to verify status and facilitate re-enrollment through Form 6.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-02/eci-orders-blos-to-re-enroll-eligible-voters-omitted-from-li.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Officials are instructed to cover at least 20-25 electors weekly, aiming to complete the process within one month. The initiative includes organizing booth-level camps and special outreach for marginalized groups, including those in labor colonies and night shelters, to ensure all eligible citizens are correctly registered.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately summarizes the ECI directive and the methodology for voter re-enrollment, capturing the key procedural details provided in the source.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/sir-eci-asks-blos-to-revisit-deleted-list-ensure-those-eligible-but-left-out-are-re-enrolled-within-a-month/article71535882.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
       <div class="sharebar" data-href="/article/2026-10-02/eci-orders-blos-to-re-enroll-eligible-voters-omitted-from-li" data-title="ECI Orders BLOs to Re-enroll Eligible Voters Omitted from Lists"><b>Share:</b>
