       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">EDUCATION</span> · Education (aggregate) · 2026-10-02 · editor 8/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Education Ministry Launches Rs 5.4 Crore Innovation Challenge</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Education</span> <span>#Innovation</span> <span>#Ministry</span> <span>#Challenge</span></div>
       <p>The Education Ministry has announced a new challenge for individuals with innovative ideas, offering a total prize fund of Rs 5.4 crore. This initiative aims to foster creativity and support groundbreaking concepts across various fields.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-02/education-ministry-launches-rs-54-crore-innovation-challenge.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Potential applicants are invited to submit their innovative ideas to the Ministry. The challenge seeks to identify and promote solutions that can contribute to advancements and address existing societal needs.</p><p>Further details regarding eligibility criteria, application procedures, and specific deadlines are expected to be released by the Education Ministry. This programme underscores the government's commitment to encouraging innovation and supporting new talent.</p><p>What to watch: Official Ministry of Education announcements for application details.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article is accurate based on the brief source provided, though it remains quite thin as the source itself is minimal.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://news.google.?oc=5" rel="noopener">Education (aggregate)</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
