     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · News18 India · 2026-10-02 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Election Commission Orders Targeted Voter Roll Verification</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The Election Commission has directed Booth Level Officers in 20 states and Union Territories to compare pre- and post-SIR electoral rolls to identify missing voters. BLOs must conduct house-to-house visits to verify the status of these individuals and assist eligible citizens in filing Form 6 for re-enrolment.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-02/election-commission-orders-targeted-voter-roll-verification.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The month-long exercise requires BLOs to share booth-wise lists of missing electors with political party representatives to facilitate transparency. This directive, part of a broader drive to enroll first-time and left-out voters, aims to rectify discrepancies identified after the Special Intensive Revision process.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article is accurate and well-synthesized, though it omits the detail regarding the specific weekly quota of 20-25 electors per BLO.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.news18.com/india/sir-audit-blos-to-match-old-new-voter-rolls-share-missing-names-with-political-parties-ws-kl-10363939.html" rel="noopener">News18 India</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
