       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">ENVIRONMENT</span> · Guardian Environment · 2026-10-02 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Extreme Weather Disrupts Spain and Nepal</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#environment</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Eastern Spain is bracing for severe flooding as a 'Dana' weather pattern moves over the region, with forecasts predicting up to 300mm of rain. Authorities in Valencia have closed schools, while three towns in Catalonia face lockdown measures due to the risk of violent thunderstorms.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-02/extreme-weather-disrupts-spain-and-nepal.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Simultaneously, Nepal continues to recover from a week of intense rainfall that triggered 542 disasters, including 304 landslides, resulting in 27 deaths. Nearly one million people received flood warnings, and 2,000 residents were relocated. Heavy rains also caused the Gandak River in India to reach record levels, while a separate nor'easter storm impacted the north-east US, leaving 200,000 without power.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article effectively synthesizes the multi-region weather reporting from the source, capturing the key figures and events accurately.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/oct/02/weather-tracker-eastern-spain-torrential-rain-flooding-nepal-landslides" rel="noopener">Guardian Environment</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
