       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · News18 India · 2026-10-02 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Family Defers Discussion of Cockpit Attack During Pilot's Recovery</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Sonal Machchhar confirmed that she and her family have not yet discussed the recent cockpit attack with her husband, Captain Smit Machchhar, to protect his mental recovery. The pilot, who suffered severe stab wounds to his head, neck, and hands, is currently recovering in an Abu Dhabi hospital following emergency surgery in Saudi Arabia.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-02/family-defers-discussion-of-cockpit-attack-during-pilots-rec.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>On September 30, a mid-air struggle occurred on flydubai flight FZ1073 when the co-pilot allegedly attacked the captain, causing the plane to plunge 14,000 feet. The captain, who recently spoke with Prime Minister Narendra Modi, managed to unlatch the door, allowing crew to subdue the attacker and safely land the aircraft.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Captures the core narrative from the source effectively with solid detail.</p>
