     <article class="story single" data-beat="sports">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">SPORTS</span> · NDTV Sports · 2026-10-02 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Gaza War Protests Interrupt Ireland-Austria Nations League Match in Dublin</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Nations League</span> <span>#Ireland</span> <span>#Austria</span> <span>#Gaza War</span></div>
       <p>The Nations League football match between Ireland and Austria in Dublin on Thursday was interrupted twice by pro-Palestine demonstrations. In the 19th minute, spectators threw tennis balls adorned with Palestinian flag stickers onto the pitch, prompting a brief halt as players exited. The game was paused again in the 35th minute when a man ran onto the field waving a Palestinian flag.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-02/gaza-war-protests-interrupt-ireland-austria-nations-league-m.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Despite the disruptions, the match concluded in a 2-2 draw. Ireland's Icelandic coach, Heimir Hallgrimsson, commented that while one is &quot;never happy with this,&quot; he understands and respects the protests. These incidents followed controversy surrounding Sunday’s Nations League match between Ireland and Israel, which was held in Hungary in a virtually empty stadium after discussions about a boycott.</p><p>During the Sunday match, which Ireland won 3-0, Irish players wore black armbands, and captains did not shake hands or exchange pennants before kick-off. The return leg between Ireland and Israel is slated for Sunday on neutral ground in Serbia, as the Football Association of Ireland deemed a home match too sensitive. Approximately 200 protesters gathered outside the Dublin Arena on Thursday evening as part of a &quot;Stop the Game&quot; campaign, criticizing the matches as &quot;sports-washing a genocide.&quot;</p><p>What to watch: The upcoming Ireland-Israel return leg and any further protests.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article provides a concise and accurate summary of the protests and match context provided in the source text.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://sports.ndtv.com/football/fiery-scenes-on-the-ground-as-gaza-war-protests-halt-ireland-austria-clash-twice-12127991#publisher=newsstand" rel="noopener">NDTV Sports</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
