     <article class="story single" data-beat="education">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">EDUCATION</span> · Education (aggregate) · 2026-10-02 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Hindu College Staff Body Alleges Irregularities, Calls for DU Takeover and Probe</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Education</span> <span>#Hindu College</span> <span>#Delhi University</span> <span>#Irregularities</span></div>
       <p>The staff body of Hindu College has raised concerns by flagging alleged irregularities within the institution. These allegations have prompted the staff to formally request intervention from Delhi University (DU), seeking its direct takeover of the college's administration.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-02/hindu-college-staff-body-alleges-irregularities-calls-for-du.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>In addition to the takeover demand, the Hindu College staff body has also called for a thorough probe into the reported issues. This action indicates a desire for a comprehensive investigation into the nature and extent of the alleged irregularities.</p><p>The development, as reported by India Today, signifies a serious internal dispute at Hindu College, with staff members urging external oversight and a detailed examination of its operations.</p><p>What to watch: Delhi University's response to the takeover request and probe demand.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Covers the essential points of the staff body's actions and demands as reported.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://news.google.?oc=5&amp;hl=en-US&amp;gl=US&amp;ceid=US:en" rel="noopener">Education (aggregate)</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
