     <article class="story single" data-beat="cricket">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">CRICKET</span> · Crictracker · 2026-10-02 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>ICC Releases 2027 World Cup Schedule, India-Pakistan Set for Potential Double Clash</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Cricket</span> <span>#World Cup</span> <span>#India</span> <span>#Pakistan</span></div>
       <p>The International Cricket Council (ICC) officially released the full schedule for the 2027 Men's Cricket World Cup on October 1, 2026. The tournament, hosted by South Africa, Zimbabwe, and Namibia, is slated to run from October 4 to November 21, 2027. A major highlight is the potential for two encounters between India and Pakistan, who are drawn into the same group and pre-seeded into the same half of the Super 7s draw.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-02/icc-releases-2027-world-cup-schedule-india-pakistan-set-for-.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The first meeting between the rivals is scheduled for the Group Stage on October 10, 2027. Following this, a second clash is set for the Super 7s phase on November 7, 2027, at Newlands Stadium in Cape Town. India leads Group A, which also includes Australia, Pakistan, Afghanistan, Zimbabwe, and Qualifier A. The Super 7s phase, running from October 25 to November 14, will see pre-seeded teams like A1 India, A2 Australia, and A3 Pakistan compete.</p><p>India's confirmed Super 7s fixtures include matches against Australia on October 28 in Victoria Falls, South Africa on October 31 in Johannesburg, and New Zealand on November 4 in Paarl, before their anticipated clash with Pakistan. Due to their placement in the same half of the Super 7s bracket, India and Pakistan cannot meet in the semi-finals, scheduled for November 17 and 18. A third encounter would only be possible if both teams reach the final on November 21 in Johannesburg.</p><p>What to watch: The potential for a blockbuster India-Pakistan final on November 21 in Johannesburg.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article is comprehensive, well-structured, and includes all relevant fixtures and logistical details provided in the source text.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.crictracker.com/cricket-news/india-and-pakistan-could-meet-for-the-second-time-in-super-7s-of-world-cup-2027-7641/" rel="noopener">Crictracker</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
