     <article class="story single" data-beat="sports">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">SPORTS</span> · NDTV Sports · 2026-10-02 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>India to Face China in Asian Games 2026 Women's Hockey Final on October 2</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Sports</span> <span>#Hockey</span> <span>#Asian Games 2026</span> <span>#India</span></div>
       <p>India's women's hockey team will compete against defending champions China in the gold medal match of the Asian Games 2026 on Friday, October 2 (IST). The high-stakes final is scheduled to take place at the Gifu Prefectural Green Stadium in Kakamigahara, with a start time of 3:30 PM IST.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-02/india-to-face-china-in-asian-games-2026-womens-hockey-final-.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Beyond the gold medal, the Asian Games champions will also secure a direct berth at the Los Angeles 2028 Olympic Games, intensifying the competition between the two unbeaten teams. India's sole women's hockey gold at the Asian Games was achieved in 1982, having settled for silver in 1998 against South Korea and in 2018 against Japan.</p><p>Spectators can watch the final live on the Sony Sports Network, with live streaming available through the SonyLIV app and website.</p><p>What to watch: Whether India can secure their second-ever Asian Games women's hockey gold and an Olympic berth.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately captures all key logistical details and historical context provided in the source.</p>
