     <article class="story single" data-beat="world">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">WORLD</span> · News18 World · 2026-10-02 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Injured Flydubai Captain Praised for Preventing Mid-Air Retaliation</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#world</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Flydubai Captain Smit Machchhar prevented passengers from attacking a co-pilot who stabbed him mid-flight on September 30, 2026. While the aircraft plummeted 17,400 feet, Machchhar instructed passengers to prioritize aircraft control over retaliation. The flight safely diverted to Tabuk, Saudi Arabia, where the captain underwent surgery before being airlifted to Abu Dhabi.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-02/injured-flydubai-captain-praised-for-preventing-mid-air-reta.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Dr. Maya Peretz, a passenger, praised Machchhar’s leadership and composure under extreme stress. Ambassador Deepak Mittal confirmed the captain is recovering well. The incident highlights the captain's focus on the safety of 174 passengers despite his serious injuries, earning widespread commendation for his humanity and presence of mind.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft effectively summarizes the provided source text regarding the incident and the captain's actions.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.news18.com/world/leave-co-pilot-focus-on-plane-flier-dr-maya-peretz-recounts-injured-captain-smit-machchhars-words-wants-daughter-to-be-like-him-ws-klrt-10364669.html" rel="noopener">News18 World</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
