       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">CRICKET</span> · ESPN Cricinfo · 2026-10-02 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Jammu &amp; Kashmir take Irani Cup first-innings lead</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#cricket</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Jammu &amp; Kashmir secured a first-innings lead of 41 runs against Rest of India during the Irani Cup match in Srinagar. Trailing by 71 runs with only two wickets remaining, J&amp;K rallied past the 237-run target set by the opposition.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-02/jammu-kashmir-take-irani-cup-first-innings-lead.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Lone Nasir contributed a pivotal 64 off 58 deliveries while batting at number ten to anchor the rearguard effort. The performance marks a turnaround for the side after bowlers successfully limited Rest of India to 237 on the opening day of play.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft accurately captures the key details of the match and the rearguard effort, though it misses the specific mention of Sunil Kumar's involvement.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
