       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">ENTERTAINMENT</span> · Variety · 2026-10-02 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Kieran Culkin Seeks Long-Term Role as Devil on 'Family Guy'</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#entertainment</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Actor Kieran Culkin expressed strong interest in maintaining his role as the Devil on the animated series &quot;Family Guy&quot; for the foreseeable future. Following his initial guest appearance, Culkin communicated to the production team that he thoroughly enjoyed the performance and wished to return to the character whenever the show revisits the Devil. </p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-02/kieran-culkin-seeks-long-term-role-as-devil-on-family-guy.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Show producers noted that Culkin was highly enthusiastic during the recording process. His proactive request to continue voicing the character signals a potential ongoing collaboration between the actor and the long-running comedy series.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft accurately captures the essence of the source material.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
