       <h1>Late Indianapolis resident bequeaths $1.6 million to Teachers' Treasures</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Terence Kahn, an Indianapolis man who lived a modest life, amassed a $13 million fortune before passing away in January 2021. Following his death, his estate representatives sought to distribute his wealth to local nonprofits.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-02/late-indianapolis-resident-bequeaths-16-million-to-teachers-.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Teachers' Treasures, an organization that provides essential supplies to educators, was selected as a beneficiary and received a $1.6 million donation. This significant contribution has enabled the nonprofit to establish its first-ever endowment fund. The gift ensures that Kahn’s accumulated wealth will continue to support the organization's mission of assisting teachers for years to come.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article is concise, accurate, and includes all the pertinent information provided in the source summary without padding or invention.</p>
