     <article class="story single" data-beat="sports">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">SPORTS</span> · NDTV Sports · 2026-10-02 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Lovlina Borgohain Secures Asian Games Gold on 29th Birthday, Joins Mary Kom</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#boxing</span> <span>#Lovlina Borgohain</span> <span>#Asian Games</span> <span>#gold medal</span></div>
       <p>Indian pugilist Lovlina Borgohain clinched a historic gold medal at the Asian Games on her 29th birthday, defeating China's Bao Ziyi by a unanimous 5-0 score. This victory makes her only the second Indian woman boxer to achieve an Asian Games gold, joining the ranks of Mary Kom.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-02/lovlina-borgohain-secures-asian-games-gold-on-29th-birthday-.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Borgohain expressed immense satisfaction, describing the gold as a self-gift for her birthday. She asserted her unwavering belief in victory despite the tough fight. She dominated the bout, securing the opening round 3-2 and the subsequent two rounds by identical 4-1 margins, earning her second Asian Games medal after a previous silver in Hangzhou.</p><p>The gold medal held particular importance for Borgohain, especially after securing a silver at the Commonwealth Games 2026. She emphasized the necessity for athletes to handle both losses and injuries, and her determination to secure this specific gold medal was paramount.</p><p>What to watch: Lovlina Borgohain's preparations and performance in future international boxing competitions.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft accurately captures the key details and quotes from the source, though it misses the minor detail about Japan being mentioned as lucky for the athlete.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://sports.ndtv.com/boxing/wanted-to-gift-myself-gold-on-my-birthday-lovlina-borgohain-after-historic-prize-at-asian-games-12128829#publisher=newsstand" rel="noopener">NDTV Sports</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
