     <article class="story single" data-beat="world">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">WORLD</span> · News18 World · 2026-10-02 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Online Theory Links Flydubai Flight Number to October 7 Anniversary</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#world</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Social media users are speculating on a connection between Flydubai flight FZ1073 and the October 7 Hamas-led attack on Israel. The number 1073 is being interpreted as 10/7/3, referencing the October 7 date and the three-year anniversary of the 2023 assault. The flight was traveling from Dubai to Tel Aviv when the Indian captain was attacked by his co-pilot.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-02/online-theory-links-flydubai-flight-number-to-october-7-anni.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>While the numerical coincidence has garnered significant attention, there is no evidence the flight number was chosen deliberately. The UAE is conducting a specialized investigation into the motives behind the cockpit assault, currently treating the incident as a potential security matter with no confirmed link to terrorist activity.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately summarizes the social media theory and the investigation status without adding external filler.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.news18.com/world/10-7-3-why-flydubai-flight-fz1073-has-triggered-a-curious-october-7-theory-online-ws-l-10364398.html" rel="noopener">News18 World</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
