       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-02 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Passenger deboarded after emergency exit alarm at Hyderabad airport</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>A passenger was deboarded from an IndiGo flight at Rajiv Gandhi International Airport in Hyderabad after accidentally triggering a security sensor alarm. The passenger, identified as Dinesh, had been moved to a seat in the emergency exit row during the boarding process.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-02/passenger-deboarded-after-emergency-exit-alarm-at-hyderabad-.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Police confirmed the action was unintentional and occurred while the man was settling into his seat. The flight, bound for Kadapa, was not delayed by the emergency exit being opened, as the passenger did not attempt to operate the door. He was handed over to the RGIA Outpost Police Station following the incident.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article is accurate and covers all essential details from the source, including the passenger's name, the location, and the nature of the incident.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.thehindu.com/news/cities/Hyderabad/passenger-deboarded-after-emergency-exit-alarm-trigger-on-indigo-flight-at-hyderabad-airport/article71535902.ece" rel="noopener">The Hindu</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
