     <article class="story single" data-beat="world">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">WORLD</span> · BBC World · 2026-10-02 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Pilot lauded after subduing co-pilot during Flydubai flight</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#world</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Capt. Smit Machchhar, an Indian pilot, successfully averted a potential disaster after his co-pilot attacked him on a Flydubai flight bound for Israel. Machchhar opened the cockpit door, allowing passengers to intervene and overpower the attacker. The pilot, who received a call from India's Prime Minister Narendra Modi, stated he fought back to ensure the safety of everyone on board.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-02/pilot-lauded-after-subduing-co-pilot-during-flydubai-flight.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>The flight departed from Dubai and landed safely in Saudi Arabia, with all passengers and crew surviving the incident. Machchhar has been widely praised as a hero for his decisive actions during the mid-air emergency.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft accurately captures the key details of the incident and the pilot's reaction.</p>
