       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · News18 India · 2026-10-02 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>PM Modi Speaks to Injured Pilot Smit Machchhar</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Sonal Machchhar, wife of Indian pilot Captain Smit Machchhar, expressed pride and gratitude after Prime Minister Narendra Modi personally called her husband. Captain Machchhar is currently recovering in an Abu Dhabi hospital from injuries sustained during a cockpit attack on a flydubai flight to Tel Aviv.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-02/pm-modi-speaks-to-injured-pilot-smit-machchhar.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>During the flight, the co-pilot allegedly stabbed the captain, who successfully opened the cockpit door to allow intervention. Sonal confirmed her husband is recovering well but stated the family is avoiding discussing the traumatic incident to prevent flashbacks. The Prime Minister's outreach has provided significant comfort to the family as they focus on the captain's full recovery.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Comprehensive and well-structured story capturing the essence of the source accurately.</p>
