     <article class="story single" data-beat="entertainment">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">ENTERTAINMENT</span> · TOI Entertainment · 2026-10-02 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Priyanka Chopra Jonas supports Fahadh Faasil’s ‘Don’t Trouble The Trouble’ on release day</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Priyanka Chopra Jonas</span> <span>#Fahadh Faasil</span> <span>#Don't Trouble The Trouble</span> <span>#Varanasi</span></div>
       <p>Priyanka Chopra Jonas expressed her support for the Telugu fantasy film ‘Don’t Trouble The Trouble’ on its release day, October 2. The actress shared the trailer on her Instagram stories, wishing producer SS Karthikeya and the team luck, and encouraging audiences to watch the film in cinemas. The movie is presented by SS Rajamouli and marks the directorial debut of Shashank Yeleti.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-02/priyanka-chopra-jonas-supports-fahadh-faasils-dont-trouble-t.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Starring Fahadh Faasil as magician Suri, the film features a storyline involving a young girl played by Ssara Palekar who is revealed to be a genie with supernatural abilities. Saurabh Sachdeva also plays a significant role in the film, which combines fantasy, adventure, and family-friendly themes. The narrative focuses on the friendship between the magician and the girl as her powers emerge.</p><p>Chopra Jonas is concurrently preparing for her return to Indian cinema with SS Rajamouli’s ‘Varanasi,’ which stars Mahesh Babu as Rudhra and Prithviraj Sukumaran as Kumbha. The film, set for a worldwide release on April 7, 2027, is described as a time-travel adventure moving from Varanasi to Antarctica and Ancient Rome. It marks the first collaboration between Babu and Rajamouli, with music by MM Keeravaani.</p><p>What to watch: Box office performance of ‘Don’t Trouble The Trouble’ and further updates on ‘Varanasi’ production.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article is well-structured and captures the essential details from the source, only missing the minor detail that Priyanka Chopra Jonas plays a character named Mandakini in the upcoming film.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/entertainment/telugu/movies/news/priyanka-chopra-jonas-lauds-fahadh-faasils-dont-trouble-the-trouble-says-go-watch-it-in-cinemas-today/articleshow/134639374.cms" rel="noopener">TOI Entertainment</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
