       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">CRICKET</span> · Crictracker · 2026-10-02 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Raza, Pooran and Moeen Ali Lead Day 3 Victories in Canada Super 60</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#cricket</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Mississauga Masters, Toronto Sixers, and Vancouver Anchors secured victories during Day 3 of the Canada Super 60 Season 2 at BC Place. Sikandar Raza starred for the undefeated Mississauga Masters, hitting a 24-ball fifty to edge Montreal Royal Tigers by two runs. Toronto Sixers chased down 128 behind Nicholas Pooran's explosive 40 off 16 balls, while the Vancouver Anchors cruised to a six-wicket win led by Moeen Ali's unbeaten 37.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-02/raza-pooran-and-moeen-ali-lead-day-3-victories-in-canada-sup.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>In the day's women's fixture, Vancouver Warriors Women defeated Vancouver Anchors Women by eight wickets. Sophie Reid anchored the chase with an unbeaten 37, successfully overhauling the Anchors' total of 81/4 in just 7.4 overs.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The report is accurate and captures all key match results, individual performances, and the women's match details from the source.</p>
