     <article class="story single" data-beat="tech">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">TECH</span> · TechCrunch · 2026-10-02 · editor 8/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Rivian Recalls R2 SUV Over Battery Pack Fastener Defect</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#tech</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Rivian has issued a recall for its R2 SUV due to improperly tightened high-voltage battery pack fasteners, which could cause power loss. The company estimates approximately 14 vehicles are affected and has already reprogrammed its assembly line in Normal, Illinois, to prevent further defects. Rivian reports no known accidents, injuries, or fatalities related to the issue.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-02/rivian-recalls-r2-suv-over-battery-pack-fastener-defect.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>This is the second recall for the R2, which launched in June as Rivian’s mass-market vehicle. The company aims to deliver 20,000 to 25,000 units by year-end to reach profitability. Affected customers will have damaged components repaired or replaced as needed.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft is accurate, though it misses the detail that the issue was identified by a manufacturing operator rather than an automated check.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://techcrunch.com/2026/10/02/rivian-issues-r2-recall-for-poorly-tightened-battery-packs/" rel="noopener">TechCrunch</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
