     <article class="story single" data-beat="cricket">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">CRICKET</span> · Crictracker · 2026-10-02 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Shubman Gill Lauds Rohit Sharma, Virat Kohli After West Indies ODI Series</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#Cricket</span> <span>#India</span> <span>#ODI</span> <span>#Shubman Gill</span></div>
       <p>India's captain, Shubman Gill, expressed profound gratitude for the presence of senior players Rohit Sharma and Virat Kohli within the squad during the ongoing ODI series against West Indies. Gill stated he feels &quot;extremely lucky&quot; to have Kohli, whom he considers the &quot;best ODI batter,&quot; and Rohit, the &quot;best ODI opener in the world,&quot; highlighting their invaluable experience.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-02/shubman-gill-lauds-rohit-sharma-virat-kohli-after-west-indie.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>India secured an eight-wicket victory in the first ODI, chasing 296 runs. In the second ODI at Barsapara Stadium in Guwahati, India successfully hunted down a 406-run target set by West Indies, with Gill himself scoring 223 not out. Virat Kohli contributed 139 not out in the first ODI, while Rohit Sharma scored a century in the second. In 2026, Rohit has amassed 512 runs in 11 ODIs, and Kohli 552 runs in 8 ODIs.</p><p>Gill adopts a consultative approach to captaincy, frequently seeking advice not only from Rohit and Virat but also from KL Rahul and Shreyas Iyer. He believes that listening to experienced voices aids him in making informed decisions on the field, ensuring all perspectives are considered before final calls.</p><p>Gill's individual performance in 2026 has been exceptional, with 894 runs in 11 ODIs (10 innings) at an average of 127.71, including 3 centuries and 5 fifties. His ODI career spans 69 matches, accumulating 3,712 runs at an average of 65.12, with 11 centuries and 20 fifties.</p><p>What to watch: India's performance in upcoming series with Gill at the helm.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article accurately captures all key quotes, statistics, and context provided in the source material.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.crictracker.com/cricket-news/i-feel-extremely-lucky-to-have-rohit-sharma-and-virat-kohli-in-team-says-shubman-gill-7598/" rel="noopener">Crictracker</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
