     <article class="story single" data-beat="national">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · India Today · 2026-10-02 · editor 6/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>South India Political Developments and Pilot Rescue Details</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>In Karnataka, the Congress government protested against alleged BJP misuse of Form 7 to manipulate electoral rolls. Meanwhile, Tamil Nadu faces intensified by-election campaigning in Madurantakam and Dharapuram, alongside a dispute over Hindi signage on highways that led to the suspension of two engineers. </p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-02/south-india-political-developments-and-pilot-rescue-details.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Separately, passenger Almog Itai recounted the mid-air rescue of Flydubai Flight FZ1073. Captain Smit Machchhar, despite suffering severe stab wounds, managed to open the cockpit door to allow passengers to assist, preventing a crash. PM Modi lauded the captain for his composure and courage, which saved 174 lives.</p>
       
       <div class="provenance">
