     <article class="story single" data-beat="finance">
       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">FINANCE</span> · Livemint Money · 2026-10-02 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>Telangana Cabinet Approves Dearness Allowance Release</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#finance</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>The Telangana Cabinet has approved the release of two pending Dearness Allowance (DA) instalments for state employees and pensioners, a move that adds ₹2,500 crore to the annual financial burden. Remaining arrears are slated for future release, though no specific timeline has been finalized.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-02/telangana-cabinet-approves-dearness-allowance-release.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Additionally, the Cabinet addressed the state's 17% rainfall deficit by forming a sub-committee to recommend drought mitigation measures and seek central assistance. Other decisions include expediting the Koheda fruit market project, cancelling several incomplete irrigation projects under the EPC scheme, and adopting a new digital media advertising policy.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article effectively synthesizes the Cabinet meeting outcomes, including the DA release, drought mitigation, and infrastructure decisions.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
      <b>Source</b>
      <ul><li><a href="https://www.livemint.com/money/da-news-telangana-cabinet-approves-release-of-two-pending-instalments-when-will-remaining-arrears-be-cleared-11790918006184.html" rel="noopener">Livemint Money</a></li></ul>
      <p>AI-generated and fact-checked against the original report; claims the gate cannot verify are held back.</p>
    </div>
       
