       <h1>UFC lightweight Bobby Green eyes 2026 record-breaking finish</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#sports</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>UFC lightweight Bobby Green, 40, is pursuing a historic fifth win of 2026 as he prepares to face Esteban Ribovics at UFC 332 this Saturday. Green enters the bout on a four-fight win streak, aiming to join an exclusive group of fighters with five calendar-year victories.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-02/ufc-lightweight-bobby-green-eyes-2026-record-breaking-finish.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Despite recent professional success, Green faced personal hardship in September when he revealed he was temporarily living out of his car. He clarified that while he is currently without his own home, he remains supported by friends and family. Green maintains that his primary focus remains providing for his loved ones, even as he continues his active fighting career.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft is accurate but thin, omitting key context like the $100,000 bonus and the specific reasons Green provided for his living situation.</p>
