       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">SCIENCE</span> · BBC Science · 2026-10-02 · editor 6/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span></div>
       <h1>UK Farmers Criticize Sustainable Farming Initiative Funding Scramble</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#science</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Farmers are expressing frustration after a £253m government funding window for the Sustainable Farming Initiative closed in less than six hours. Norfolk farmer Lex Brun reported missing out on a £100,000 grant, forcing him to reconsider environmental projects in favor of commercial crops due to rising costs.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-02/uk-farmers-criticize-sustainable-farming-initiative-funding-.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>Farming Minister Stephen Morgan acknowledged the disappointment and promised to learn from the application process, while the Country Land and Business Association warned of reduced environmental engagement. As the government considers future support, politicians and agricultural groups are calling for continued investment to ensure long-term confidence in green land management schemes.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The article misses significant context, such as the specific dates the funding window was open and the fact that the government plans to provide info on 2027 funding.</p>
