       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">NATIONAL</span> · The Hindu · 2026-10-02 · editor 9/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Yanadi and Chenchu Communities Face Severe Landlessness in Andhra Pradesh</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#national</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Marginalized Yanadi and Chenchu communities in Andhra Pradesh continue to struggle with insecure housing and extreme poverty. Despite available government welfare schemes, these groups remain detached from urban amenities and face a persistent gap in living standards compared to nearby residents.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-02/yanadi-and-chenchu-communities-face-severe-landlessness-in-a.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>In Prabhu Nagar, families reside in makeshift shelters on private land used as a burial ground. Faced with constant pressure from landowners to vacate, these residents remain in a state of deep deprivation, lacking basic infrastructure while navigating a cycle of landlessness and social neglect.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: Effectively synthesizes the detailed source material into a coherent news report.</p>
       <div class="provenance">
