       <div class="meta"><span class="beat-tag">CRICKET</span> · Crictracker · 2026-10-02 · editor 10/10 · 1 min read <span class="badge ok">fact-checked</span><span class="badge quick">quick bite</span></div>
       <h1>Yuzvendra Chahal Retires from First-Class Cricket to Focus on White-Ball Formats</h1>
       <div class="tags"><span>#cricket</span> <span>#brief</span></div>
       <p>Indian leg-spinner Yuzvendra Chahal announced his retirement from first-class cricket, concluding a red-ball career spanning 49 matches and 148 wickets, with six five-wicket hauls. Chahal made the announcement on Instagram, confirming his intention to pursue opportunities in ODI and T20 formats while stepping away from the red-ball game.</p><img class="hero-art" src="/img/2026-10-02/yuzvendra-chahal-retires-from-first-class-cricket-to-focus-o.webp" width="1200" height="675" alt="" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async"><p>His final first-class match took place at Lord's for Northamptonshire against Middlesex, concluding on September 26, 2026, where he claimed two wickets. Chahal previously represented Haryana in domestic cricket and last played internationally for India in August 2023.</p>
       <p class="critique">Editor's note: The draft effectively synthesizes the full source text, covering the statistical career data, the final match details, and the player's future intentions.</p>
